hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19234","He said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Zurarah ibn Awfa from Malik ibn al-Harith, a man of them, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever takes an orphan among two Muslim parents to his food and drink until he is independent of him, Paradise is assured for him. Whoever frees a Muslim person, it will be his ransom from the Fire, each limb of him sufficing for a limb of him from the Fire."
"19235","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan from Zurarah ibn Awfa from Amr ibn Malik or Malik ibn Amr, so Sufyan said, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes an orphan between his parents, Paradise is assured for him."
